# Demonstrates ADR-002's CHANGE keyword: SET always creates/updates the
# CURRENT scope only, so a plain SET inside REPEAT/FOR EACH re-shadows a
# fresh local every iteration and can't accumulate. CHANGE walks outward
# to the binding that already exists and mutates it in place.

SET total = 0
SET counter = 1

REPEAT 5 TIMES
    CHANGE total = total + counter
    CHANGE counter = counter + 1
END

SHOW total
